A.  Klein-Nishina differential cross-section  d(sigma)/ds
==============================================================================
   d(sigma)/ds = (pi r_e^2 / a) [ s + 1/s - 1 + cos^2(theta) ],
   cos(theta) = 1 - (1/s - 1)/a,   1/(1+2a) <= s <= 1,   a = E/m_e c^2
   [Klein & Nishina 1929; Rybicki & Lightman 1979 Eq. 7.5, with
    d(cos theta) = ds/(a s^2) so that d(sigma)/ds = d(sigma)/d(cos theta)/(a s^2)]

