     z = 10.0   kT = 2.5835e-03 eV   E_th = 1.0107e+14 eV = 101 TeV
     z = 5.5    kT = 1.5266e-03 eV   E_th = 1.7104e+14 eV = 171 TeV

   Exact Wien-tail rate (numerical, full Planck spectrum):
   z        E [eV]         1/Gamma [m]      1/Gamma [Mpc]
   20.0     1e+12          1.7237e+38       5.5862e+15
   20.0     1e+13          9.7858e+17       3.1713e-05
   20.0     1e+14          2.3328e+16       7.5602e-07
   10.0     1e+12          inf              inf
   10.0     1e+13          6.7185e+20       2.1773e-02
   10.0     1e+14          1.9906e+17       6.4512e-06

   Onset criterion:  1/Gamma_gg(E, z_i)  <  proper light path
   z_i      light path [m]   E_gg [eV]        E_gg [TeV]
   20.0     8.1393e+24       2.4411e+12       2.441
   15.0     7.2862e+24       3.3301e+12       3.33
   10.0     5.3645e+24       5.2501e+12       5.25
   7.0      2.6288e+24       7.8723e+12       7.872

   So the E > 2.4e+12 eV end of the grid is ALSO a lower bound: there
   the photon pair-produces on the CMB well inside the window, and
   the resulting e+e- pair inverse-Compton-cools and ionizes.  The
   two omitted channels therefore bracket the trustworthy range as
     13.6 eV  <  E  <  3.68e+07 eV   (yield exact)
   and mark everything outside it as a lower bound.

